; spire(1): the art, as a script in tiles(2)'s command language.  The
; game runs this file line by line at start-up; none of it is compiled
; in.  The surfaces are made in the program because their size depends
; on how tall the tower is.

sheet tower /lib/tiles/spire.chr
sheet16 folk /lib/tiles/spire16.chr
font text

palette psky   mid.azure  mid.azure   pale.grey   light.grey
palette pstone mid.azure  dark.violet mid.violet  light.violet
palette pledge mid.azure  dark.grey   light.grey  pale.grey
palette pdoor  mid.azure  dark.black  mid.orange  light.yellow
palette pcoin  mid.azure  dark.yellow pale.yellow mid.yellow
palette pcloud mid.azure  light.grey  pale.grey   pale.grey
palette pgoal  mid.azure  dark.yellow pale.yellow light.yellow
palette pyou   mid.azure  dark.black  pale.rose   mid.cyan
palette pfoe   mid.azure  dark.black  mid.green   light.lime
palette phud   dark.black pale.grey   pale.grey   pale.grey
palette pwarn  dark.black light.red   light.red   light.red
palette pgood  dark.black light.lime  light.lime  light.lime

; Colours that belong to no tile, declared the way the command language
; names a colour: as a palette whose first entry is the one wanted.
palette csky   mid.azure  mid.azure   mid.azure   mid.azure
palette cpanel dark.black dark.black  dark.black  dark.black
